note as N1
  update() order (runs every egui frame)
  1. poll_export_job(): drain the worker channel, update ExportProgressModal, on Finished/Failed close it and (Failed) open ErrorModal.
  2. If screen is Editor: playback.tick(now) (may change the selected frame, then ctx.request_repaint_after(next_deadline)).
  3. Draw the current screen (WelcomeScreen::ui or EditorScreen::ui) -> Vec<AppAction> (blocked from input while a modal is open).
  4. Draw the modal (if any) centred, with a dimming layer over the screen. ModalOutcome::Accepted(action) / Cancelled closes it.
  5. for each AppAction collected in 3 and 4 -> handle_action(). Actions never run inside the draw code (no re-entrancy).
  on_close_requested(): if Editor and session.history.is_dirty() -> cancel the OS close, pending = QuitApplication,
  open ConfirmUnsavedModal; otherwise allow the close. If an export job is running: set its cancel flag, join the worker, then allow the close.
  Only ONE modal exists at a time. Opening a modal while one is open replaces it, EXCEPT ErrorModal which is shown
  after the current modal is closed (it replaces the current one only when the current one is NewProject/Save and the
  error came from its own action).
end note

note as N2
  - original / working: Option<Rgb>. None means "transparent" and is only offered when allow_transparent (= EraseColor target).
  - UI: RGB sliders 0-255, hex field (#RRGGBB, validated live with Rgb::from_hex), 16 preset swatches, old/new preview.
  - "Apply to all frames" checkbox is only shown for ColorPickTarget::FrameBackground.
  - OK -> Accepted(ApplyColor(target, working, apply_to_all)).  Cancel / Esc -> Cancelled (nothing changes).
end note

note as N3
  Fields and validation (validate() runs when Create is pressed; the Create button is disabled while the form is invalid)
  - name: trimmed, 1..=64 chars, none of  / \ : * ? " < > |  and not ending with '.' or ' '. Default "Untitled".
  - folder: must exist and be writable. Default = <Documents>/AsciiPaint (created if missing). "Browse..." uses a native folder dialog.
  - target file = folder/name.aspr must NOT exist -> error "A project with this name already exists in this folder."
  - background: initial background colour of frame 1 (default #000000), edited with the same ColorPickerModal-style widget inline.
  - fps: 1..=60 (default 12).
  - canvas: shown read-only as "240 x 72 cells - 8 x 15 px" (not editable in this milestone).
end note

note as N4
  - Format list grouped by scope:  Project: .aspr  |  Current frame: .png, .ascii  |  All frames: .aanim, .mp4.
  - AnimationMp4 is disabled (greyed, tooltip "ffmpeg not found") when FfmpegLocator::find() returned None.
  - Default file name = project name (+ "_frame" + 3-digit 1-based index for FramePng / FrameAscii); extension follows the format.
  - Save is enabled when folder exists, file_name is a valid file name (same rules as project name) .
  - If the file already exists a confirmation line "File exists - it will be replaced" is shown (no extra dialog).
end note


