note as N1
  EditorSession is the single source of truth while a project is open. UI widgets mutate it ONLY through these methods.
  - add_frame()/duplicate_frame()/delete_frame()/move_frame(): build the matching Command (05), history.execute(), stop playback.
  - set_frame_background(id, c, all_frames): all_frames=false -> SetFrameBackgroundCommand (skipped when colour unchanged);
      all_frames=true -> CompositeCommand of one SetFrameBackgroundCommand per differing frame. history.execute().
  - set_fps() / set_looping(): SetPlaybackSettingsCommand. select_frame(i): timeline.select(i) (not undoable), keeps the selection mask.
  - undo()/redo(): see History rules; they also stop playback first.
  - delete_selection_contents(): when selection is non-empty, clears every selected cell of the current frame
      with ClearOperation inside ONE PatchBuilder ("Clear selection").
  - toggle_playback(): see state diagram 11 (playback). Starting playback cancels any busy tool.
end note

note as N2
  Geometry (page = canvas.pixel_width x canvas.pixel_height "page pixels", origin = screen position of the page top-left
  relative to the canvas widget's top-left)
  - page_px = (screen - view.min - origin) / zoom
  - cell    = (floor(page_px.x / cell_w), floor(page_px.y / cell_h)); None when outside 0..cols / 0..rows.
  - cell_rect(c) = [origin + (c.col*cell_w, c.row*cell_h)*zoom, size (cell_w, cell_h)*zoom] in widget coordinates.
  - zoom_at(cursor, notches): z' = clamp(zoom * WHEEL_STEP^notches, MIN_ZOOM, MAX_ZOOM);
      origin' = (cursor - view.min) - ((cursor - view.min) - origin) * (z' / zoom); zoom = z'.   (point under cursor stays fixed)
  - pan_by(d): origin += d, then clamp so that at least 64 screen px of the page stay visible on each axis.
  - fit(): zoom = clamp(min(view.w / page_w, view.h / page_h) * 0.95, MIN, MAX); page centred in the view.
  - actual_size(): zoom = 1.0 (1 page pixel = 1 screen pixel); page centred.
  - zoom_step(+1/-1): z' = clamp(zoom * 1.25^dir) around the view centre. A new Editor opens with fit().
end note

note as N3
  Input mapping (translate_input)
  - Mouse wheel over the canvas = zoom_at(cursor, scroll_y / 50.0). (Never scrolls.)
  - Middle-button drag, or Space held + left drag = pan_by(drag delta). Space-pan suppresses tool events.
  - Primary button -> ToolEvent::PointerDown / PointerMove / PointerUp / DoubleClick with cell = screen_to_cell(...).
  - Typed text (egui Event::Text, printable only) -> ToolEvent::Text; Enter/Backspace/Delete/Arrows/Escape -> ToolEvent::Key.
    Only when the canvas has keyboard focus (clicking the canvas gives focus; text fields elsewhere take it away).
  - Returns the hovered cell for the StatusBar.
  - Painting order: see CanvasRenderer note.
end note

note as N4
  paint() draw order (only the cells returned by Viewport::visible_cells are visited)
  1. Dark neutral workspace fill (#2B2B2B) over the whole widget.
  2. PAGE: filled rect with timeline.selected_frame().background.
  3. For each visible cell: if bg = Some(c) fill cell rect with c.
  4. For each visible cell with glyph != ' ': textured quad from GlyphAtlas::uv(glyph), tinted with fg.
  5. Grid lines (1 px, white at 12% opacity) when show_grid && zoom >= 2.0.
  6. Selection: boundary_edges() (cached by Selection::revision) as 1.5 px dashed black/white "marching ants".
  7. Tool overlay: text cursor (blinking 500 ms), rect/ellipse preview, polygon rubber-band, hovered-cell outline.
  8. Page border (1 px #000000 at 60%).
  While Playing, steps 6-7 are skipped. The glyph cache key is only the char, the colour is applied by the vertex tint.
end note

note as N5
  tick(now, tl) -> Option<Duration> = time until the next frame change (for ctx.request_repaint_after) or None when Stopped.
  See the Playback state machine (11) for the exact transitions.
end note

note as N6
  Layout (top to bottom): header "Frames" | scrollable list of FrameItem | [+ Add] [Duplicate] [Delete] |
  separator | "Background" swatch + hex text of the SELECTED frame | FPS field | [Play/Pause] [x] Loop.
  - FrameItem = 1-based index label + thumbnail (ThumbnailCache) + highlight when selected. Click = select_frame(i).
  - Drag a FrameItem: FrameDrag{from, hover_slot}; on release, if hover_slot != from -> move_frame(from, to).
  - Delete is disabled when timeline.len() == 1. Add inserts AFTER the selected frame and selects it.
  - Background swatch click -> AppAction::OpenColorPicker(ColorPickTarget::FrameBackground(selected frame id)).
    The hex field commits on Enter / focus loss (valid #RRGGBB only, otherwise reverts) via set_frame_background(id, c, false).
  - FPS = DragValue 1..=60 integer, commits via set_fps() (Enter / focus loss / drag release). Loop checkbox -> set_looping().
  - All edit buttons are disabled while Playing, except Play/Pause itself and frame selection (which stops playback).
end note


